id: pm-rlm-github-dfe63798395a-5
title: Checkpoint validation rejects engine-generated empty response steps and blocks recovery
description: "GH issue #5: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/issues/5 · author @unbraind · state reason completed · created 2026-10-19T00:32:53Z · updated 2026-10-19T05:49:22Z"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rlm#5","github_author:unbraind"
created_at: "2026-10-20T08:34:35.999Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T08:34:36.068Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-20T08:34:36.065Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-19T05:49:22.000Z"
author: pm-github
close_reason: GitHub issue #5 closed
body: "The new checkpoint validation in PR #2 at `aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0` rejects a checkpoint that the same engine successfully writes when a supported custom `RlmModel` returns an empty string. A subsequent valid finish can return success, but replay and resume both fail with `RlmError { code: 'incomplete', message: 'Run checkpoint is invalid' }`. An interrupted run with the same recorded empty-response refusal also cannot resume.\n\n## Contract and cause\n\n- [README](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0/README.md#L80-L90) explicitly supports implementing `RlmModel` and says invalid JSON becomes a recorded refusal that spends a reserved step\n- [The engine](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0/src/engine.ts#L141-L164) accepts string response text, including `''`, checkpoints it, and records `{ refused: 'invalid' }` after JSON parsing fails\n- [The new loader](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0/src/ledger.ts#L78-L86) calls `text(response.text)`, which requires a nonempty string. It therefore classifies this engine-generated checkpoint as corrupt\n\nThis affects the documented third-party model interface. The built-in HTTP adapter already rejects empty model text before writing it, so this is not a claim that ordinary Ollama/OpenAI-compatible runs necessarily hit the problem.\n\n## Minimal regression\n\nSave this as a test under `test/` and run it with Node's test runner in the project checkout:\n\n```ts\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { test } from 'node:test';\nimport { runRlm, replayRlm, resumeRlm } from '../src/engine.ts';\nimport { tracker, ScriptedModel } from './helpers.ts';\n\ntest('empty model output remains a replayable refusal', async t => {\n  const { workspace } = await tracker(t);\n  const model = new ScriptedModel((_request, index) =>\n    index === 0 ? '' : '{\"action\":\"finish\",\"answer\":\"ok\"}');\n  const result = await runRlm('Recover from invalid JSON', { workspace, model });\n  assert.equal(result.answer, 'ok');\n  assert.equal(model.requests.length, 2);\n  assert.equal((await replayRlm(workspace, result.run)).answer, 'ok');\n  const noInference = new ScriptedModel(() => {\n    throw new Error('Completed resume must not infer');\n  });\n  assert.equal((await resumeRlm(workspace, result.run, noInference)).answer, 'ok');\n  assert.equal(noInference.requests.length, 0);\n});\n```\n\n## Independent verification\n\nUsing Node 24.19.0, unchanged locked dependencies and real SDK scratch trackers, four contract cases were tested on exact source:\n\n- Prior head `76a20eb8d1920258dd3218d76f91147484406539`: 4/4 pass\n- New head `aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0`: 2/4 pass; the completed and interrupted empty-response cases fail\n- Controls with nonempty malformed JSON (`'{'`) and whitespace (`' '`) pass on the new head\n- A separate diagnostic copy changing only response-text validation to accept strings, including empty strings, passes 4/4; its existing round-2 malformed-checkpoint/settings suite still passes 6/6\n\nThe new head's existing 91-test suite passes, so this edge case is currently uncovered. No external model calls or production data were used.\n\nPlease align loaded response-text validation with the writer and the documented malformed-action recovery semantics, preserving rejection of non-string response values. Keep a regression for both completed replay/resume and interrupted recovery. This is distinct from repaired issue #4 (failed recursive children) and the existing interrupted-spawn observation review thread: the minimal reproduction has one root call, and fails in `load` before replay traverses any action."
